<title>USA: Signet Group halts jewelry unit's sale talks.</title>
<headline>Signet Group halts jewelry unit's sale talks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Signet Group Plc said Thursday said it has ended talks to sell its United Kingdom jewelry business.</p>
<p>The company said it entertained several offers and negotiated with one potential buyer.</p>
<p>But, it said, it was unable to secure a &quot;satisfactory agreement&quot; on the structure and terms of a potential sale, and decided to end the negotiations.</p>
<p>Signet Group Plc is a British retailer of jewelry, watches and gifts trading in the United Kingdom as H. Samuel and Ernest Jones, and in the U.S. as Sterling.</p>
</text>
